Article 2 The following activities conducted within the territory of the People's Republic of China shall comply with this Law:
(1) Food production and processing (hereinafter referred to as food production), food sales and catering services (hereinafter referred to as food trading);
(2) Production and trading of food additives;
(3) Production and trading of packaging materials, containers, detergents, disinfectants, and tools and equipment used for food production and trading (hereinafter referred to as food-related products);
(4) Use of food additives and food-related products by food producers and traders;
(5) Storage and transportation of food;
(6) Safety management of food, food additives, and food-related products.
The quality and safety management of primary agricultural products for consumption (hereinafter referred to as edible agricultural products) shall comply with the provisions of the Agricultural Product Quality Safety Law of the People's Republic of China. However, the market sale of edible agricultural products, the formulation of relevant quality and safety standards, the publication of relevant safety information, and where this Law provides for agricultural inputs, the provisions of this Law shall be complied with.

Article 18 A food safety risk assessment shall be conducted under any of the following circumstances:
(1) Where through food safety risk monitoring or upon receipt of reports, it is found that food, food additives, or food-related products may have potential safety hazards;
(2) Where a risk assessment is needed to provide a scientific basis for formulating or revising national food safety standards;
(3) Where a risk assessment is needed to determine key areas and key varieties for supervision and administration;
(4) Where new factors that may endanger food safety are discovered;
(5) Where it is necessary to determine whether a certain factor constitutes a potential food safety hazard; or
(6) Other circumstances where the health administration department of the State Council considers a risk assessment necessary.

Article 26 Food safety standards shall include the following:
(1) Limit provisions on pathogenic microorganisms, pesticide residues, veterinary drug residues, biotoxins, heavy metals and other pollutants, as well as other substances harmful to human health in food, food additives, and food-related products;
(2) Varieties, scope of use, and dosage of food additives;
(3) Nutritional requirements for staple and supplementary foods exclusively for infants and other specific groups;
(4) Requirements on labels, markings, and instructions related to hygiene, nutrition, and other food safety requirements;
(5) Hygiene requirements in the process of food production and business operations;
(6) Quality requirements related to food safety;
(7) Food inspection methods and procedures related to food safety; and
(8) Other contents that need to be developed as food safety standards.

Article 100 The national entry-exit inspection and quarantine department shall collect and compile the following import and export food safety information and promptly notify the relevant departments, agencies, and enterprises:
(1) Food safety information discovered by the entry-exit inspection and quarantine authorities during inspection and quarantine of imported and exported food;
(2) Information on imported food safety reflected by food industry associations, consumer associations, and other organizations, and consumers;
(3) Risk warning information and other food safety information released by international organizations and overseas governmental agencies, as well as food safety information reflected by overseas food industry associations and other organizations, and consumers;
(4) Other food safety information.
The national entry-exit inspection and quarantine department shall implement credit management for importers, exporters, and exported food manufacturers of imported and exported food, establish credit records, and publicly disclose them to the public according to law. For importers, exporters, and exported food manufacturers with adverse records, the inspection and quarantine of their imported and exported food shall be strengthened.

Article 105 Upon receiving a report of a food safety incident, the food safety supervision and administration department of a people's government at or above the county level shall immediately, jointly with the health administrative department, the agricultural administrative department, and other departments at the same level, investigate and handle the incident, and take the following measures to prevent or mitigate social harm:
(1) Carry out emergency rescue work and organize the treatment of persons injured due to the food safety incident;
(2) Seal up food and its raw materials that may have caused the food safety incident and immediately conduct inspection; if it is confirmed that the food and its raw materials are contaminated, order the food producer or business operator to recall or stop the operation in accordance with the provisions of Article 63 of this Law;
(3) Seal up the contaminated food-related products and order cleaning and disinfection;
(4) Properly carry out information release, release information on the food safety incident and its handling according to law, and explain and illustrate the possible harm.
If a food safety incident requires the activation of a contingency plan, the people's government at or above the county level shall immediately establish an incident handling command organization, activate the contingency plan, and handle the incident in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph and the contingency plan.
When a food safety incident occurs, the disease prevention and control institution at or above the county level shall conduct sanitary treatment at the incident site and carry out epidemiological investigations on factors related to the incident, and relevant departments shall provide assistance. The disease prevention and control institution at or above the county level shall submit an epidemiological investigation report to the food safety supervision and administration department and the health administrative department at the same level.

Article 109 The food safety supervision and administration department of a people's government at or above the county level shall, based on food safety risk monitoring results, risk assessment results, and the food safety situation, determine the priorities, methods, and frequency of supervision and administration, and implement risk-graded management.
The local people's government at or above the county level shall organize the food safety supervision and administration department, the agricultural administrative department, and other departments at the same level to formulate an annual supervision and administration plan for food safety within its administrative region, publish it to the public, and organize its implementation.
The annual supervision and administration plan for food safety shall take the following matters as the priorities of supervision and administration:
(1) Staple and supplementary foods exclusively for infants and young children and other specific populations;
(2) The addition behavior in the production process of health food and the situation of organizing production according to the technical requirements for registration or recordation, and the situation of functional claims in health food labels, instructions, and promotional materials;
(3) Food producers and business operators with a higher risk of food safety incidents;
(4) Matters for which food safety risk monitoring results indicate potential food safety hazards.

Article 110 When performing the duties of food safety supervision and administration, the food safety supervision and administration department of a people's government at or above the county level shall have the authority to take the following measures to supervise and inspect whether producers and business operators comply with this Law:
(1) Enter the production and business operation premises to conduct on-site inspections;
(2) Conduct sample inspections of food, food additives, and food-related products being produced or sold;
(3) Consult and copy relevant contracts, invoices, account books, and other relevant materials;
(4) Seal up or seize food, food additives, and food-related products for which there is evidence that they do not comply with food safety standards or for which there is evidence of potential safety hazards, and which are used for illegal production and business operations;
(5) Seal up premises used for illegal production and business operations.

Article 123 Whoever, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commits any of the following acts, if the act does not constitute a crime, the food safety supervision and administration department of the people's government at or above the county level shall confiscate the illegal gains and the illegally produced or operated food, and may also confiscate the tools, equipment, raw materials and other articles used for the illegal production or business operation; if the value of the illegally produced or operated food is less than 10,000 yuan, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 150,000 yuan shall also be imposed; if the value is 10,000 yuan or more, a fine of not less than 15 times but not more than 30 times the value shall also be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the license shall be revoked, and the public security organ may impose detention of not less than five days but not more than 15 days on the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons:
(1) Producing food with non-food raw materials, adding chemical substances other than food additives and other substances that may be harmful to human health to food, or producing food with recycled food as raw materials, or operating the aforesaid food;
(2) Producing or operating staple or supplementary foods exclusively for infants and young children and other specific groups of people whose nutritional contents do not meet the food safety standards;
(3) Operating the meat of poultry, livestock, animals or aquatic animals that die of disease, poisoning or unknown causes, or producing or operating their products;
(4) Operating meat that has not undergone quarantine as required or has failed quarantine, or producing or operating meat products that have not undergone inspection or have failed inspection;
(5) Producing or operating food that the state expressly prohibits from production or operation for special needs such as disease prevention;
(6) Producing or operating food to which drugs have been added.
Whoever knowingly provides premises or other conditions for the illegal act specified in the preceding paragraph shall be ordered by the food safety supervision and administration department of the people's government at or above the county level to cease the illegal act, have the illegal gains confiscated, and be imposed a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the legitimate rights and interests of consumers are harmed, such person shall bear joint and several liability with the food producer or business operator.
Whoever illegally uses highly toxic or acutely toxic pesticides shall, in addition to being punished in accordance with relevant laws and regulations, be subject to detention by the public security organ in accordance with the provisions of the first paragraph.

Article 124 Whoever, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commits any of the following acts, if the act does not constitute a crime, the food safety supervision and administration department of the people's government at or above the county level shall confiscate the illegal gains and the illegally produced or operated food and food additives, and may also confiscate the tools, equipment, raw materials and other articles used for the illegal production or business operation; if the value of the illegally produced or operated food and food additives is less than 10,000 yuan, a fine of not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall also be imposed; if the value is 10,000 yuan or more, a fine of not less than 10 times but not more than 20 times the value shall also be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the license shall be revoked:
(1) Producing or operating food or food additives in which the content of pathogenic microorganisms, pesticide residues, veterinary drug residues, biotoxins, heavy metals and other pollutants, or other substances harmful to human health exceeds the limits specified in food safety standards;
(2) Using food raw materials or food additives that have exceeded the shelf life to produce food or food additives, or operating the aforesaid food or food additives;
(3) Producing or operating food in which the use of food additives exceeds the scope or limit;
(4) Producing or operating food or food additives that are deteriorated, rancid, moldy, infested with insects, filthy, mixed with foreign matters, adulterated, or abnormal in sensory properties;
(5) Producing or operating food or food additives with false labels of production date and shelf life, or that have exceeded the shelf life;
(6) Producing or operating health food, formula food for special medical purposes, infant formula milk powder, or infant formula liquid milk that have not been registered in accordance with the provisions, or failing to organize production in accordance with the registered product formulas, production processes and other technical requirements;
(7) Producing infant formula milk powder or infant formula liquid milk by repackaging, or producing infant formula milk powder or infant formula liquid milk of different brands with the same formula by the same enterprise;
(8) Using new food raw materials to produce food, or producing new varieties of food additives, without passing the safety assessment;
(9) After being ordered by the food safety supervision and administration department to recall or cease operation, a food producer or business operator refuses to recall or cease operation.
Except for the circumstances specified in the preceding paragraph and Articles 123 and 125 of this Law, whoever produces or operates food or food additives that do not comply with laws, regulations or food safety standards shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.
Whoever produces new varieties of food-related products without passing the safety assessment, or produces food-related products that do not comply with food safety standards, shall be punished by the food safety supervision and administration department of the people's government at or above the county level in accordance with the provisions of the first paragraph.

Article 125 Whoever, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the food safety supervision and administration department of the people's government at or above the county level shall confiscate the illegal gains and the illegally produced or operated food and food additives, and may also confiscate the tools, equipment, raw materials and other articles used for the illegal production or business operation; if the value of the illegally produced or operated food and food additives is less than 10,000 yuan, a fine of not less than 5,000 yuan but not more than 50,000 yuan shall also be imposed; if the value is 10,000 yuan or more, a fine of not less than 5 times but not more than 10 times the value shall also be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the production or business operation shall be ordered to suspend for rectification, until the license is revoked:
(1) Producing or operating food or food additives contaminated by packaging materials, containers, means of transport, etc.;
(2) Producing or operating pre-packaged food or food additives without labels, or food or food additives whose labels or instructions do not comply with the provisions of this Law;
(3) Producing or operating genetically modified food without labeling as required;
(4) A food producer or business operator purchases or uses food raw materials, food additives, or food-related products that do not comply with food safety standards.
Where the labels or instructions of the produced or operated food or food additives have defects but do not affect food safety and are not likely to mislead consumers, the food safety supervision and administration department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order corrective action; if correction is refused, a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan shall be imposed.

Article 126 Whoever, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the food safety supervision and administration department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order corrective action and give a warning; if correction is refused, a fine of not less than 5,000 yuan but not more than 50,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the production or business operation shall be ordered to suspend for rectification, until the license is revoked:
(1) A food or food additive producer fails to inspect purchased food raw materials and the produced food or food additives as required;
(2) A food production or business operation enterprise fails to establish a food safety management system as required, or fails to equip or train or assess food safety management personnel as required;
(3) A food or food additive producer or business operator fails to examine the license and relevant certification documents when purchasing goods, or fails to establish and comply with the purchasing inspection record, factory inspection record and sales record system as required;
(4) A food production or business operation enterprise fails to formulate a food safety accident handling plan;
(5) Tableware, drinking utensils and containers for directly consumed food are not cleaned or disinfected before use or the cleaning and disinfection are not up to standard, or the catering service facilities and equipment are not regularly maintained, cleaned or verified as required;
(6) A food producer or business operator arranges persons who have not obtained a health certificate or who suffer from diseases that may affect food safety as prescribed by the health administrative department of the State Council to engage in work involving direct contact with food;
(7) A food business operator fails to sell food in accordance with the provisions;
(8) A health food production enterprise fails to file with the food safety supervision and administration department as required, or fails to organize production in accordance with the filed product formula, production process and other technical requirements;
(9) An infant formula food production enterprise fails to file the food raw materials, food additives, product formulas, labels, etc. with the food safety supervision and administration department;
(10) A special food production enterprise fails to establish a production quality management system and operate it effectively as required, or fails to submit a self-inspection report on a regular basis;
(11) A food producer or business operator fails to regularly inspect and evaluate the food safety status, or fails to handle changes in production or business operation conditions as required;
(12) A centralized dining unit such as a school, nursery, kindergarten, elderly care institution or construction site fails to perform the food safety management responsibility as required;
(13) A food production enterprise or catering service provider fails to formulate and implement the control requirements for the production or business operation process as required.
Where a centralized disinfection service unit for tableware and drinking utensils uses water, detergents or disinfectants in violation of the provisions of this Law, or fails to inspect the tableware and drinking utensils leaving the factory as required and attach the disinfection qualification certificate, or fails to mark the relevant contents on the individual packaging as required, the health administrative department of the people's government at or above the county level shall impose punishment in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.
Where a food-related product producer fails to inspect the produced food-related products as required, the food safety supervision and administration department of the people's government at or above the county level shall impose punishment in accordance with the provisions of the first paragraph.
Where an edible agricultural product seller violates the provisions of Article 65 of this Law, the food safety supervision and administration department of the people's government at or above the county level shall impose punishment in accordance with the provisions of the first paragraph.

Article 129 Whoever, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the entry-exit inspection and quarantine authority shall impose punishment in accordance with the provisions of Article 124 of this Law:
(1) Providing false materials, importing food, food additives or food-related products that do not comply with the national food safety standards of China;
(2) Importing food for which there are no national food safety standards, without submitting the standard implemented and having it reviewed by the health administrative department of the State Council, or importing food produced with new food raw materials, importing new varieties of food additives or new varieties of food-related products without passing the safety assessment;
(3) Failing to comply with the provisions of this Law when exporting food;
(4) After being ordered by the relevant competent department to recall the imported food in accordance with the provisions of this Law, the importer still refuses to recall.
Where, in violation of the provisions of this Law, an importer fails to establish and comply with the record system for the import and sale of food and food additives, or the audit system for overseas exporters or production enterprises, the entry-exit inspection and quarantine authority shall impose punishment in accordance with the provisions of Article 126 of this Law.

Article 142 In violation of the provisions of this Law, where the local people's government at or above the county level commits any of the following acts, the directly responsible persons in charge and other directly liable persons shall be given the sanction of a major demerit; if the circumstances are relatively serious, the sanction of demotion or removal from office shall be given; if the circumstances are serious, the sanction of expulsion shall be given; if serious consequences are caused, the principal responsible person shall also resign to assume responsibility:

(1) failing to timely organize and coordinate the relevant departments to carry out effective handling of a food safety accident occurring within its administrative region, resulting in adverse effects or losses;

(2) failing to timely organize rectification of regional food safety issues involving multiple links within its administrative region, resulting in adverse effects or losses;

(3) concealing, falsely reporting, or delaying the reporting of a food safety accident;

(4) a particularly major food safety accident occurring within its administrative region, or a continuous occurrence of major food safety accidents.

Article 143 In violation of the provisions of this Law, where the local people's government at or above the county level commits any of the following acts, the directly responsible persons in charge and other directly liable persons shall be given the sanction of a warning, a demerit, or a major demerit; if serious consequences are caused, the sanction of demotion or removal from office shall be given:

(1) failing to determine the food safety supervision and administration functions and duties of the relevant departments, failing to establish and improve the whole-process food safety supervision and administration mechanism and information sharing mechanism, or failing to implement the food safety supervision and administration responsibility system;

(2) failing to formulate an emergency plan for food safety accidents within its administrative region, or, after a food safety accident occurs, failing to immediately establish an accident handling command structure and activate the emergency plan as required.

Article 144 In violation of the provisions of this Law, where the food safety supervision and administration, health administration, and agricultural administration departments of the people's government at or above the county level commit any of the following acts, the directly responsible persons in charge and other directly liable persons shall be given the sanction of a major demerit; if the circumstances are relatively serious, the sanction of demotion or removal from office shall be given; if the circumstances are serious, the sanction of expulsion shall be given; if serious consequences are caused, the principal responsible person shall also resign to assume responsibility:

(1) concealing, falsely reporting, or delaying the reporting of a food safety accident;

(2) failing to investigate and handle a food safety accident as required, or failing to handle a food safety accident report in a timely manner after receiving it, resulting in the expansion or spread of the accident;

(3) after obtaining a conclusion from a food safety risk assessment that food, food additives, or food-related products are unsafe, failing to take corresponding measures in a timely manner, resulting in a food safety accident or adverse social impacts;

(4) granting a permit to an applicant who does not meet the conditions, or granting a permit beyond the statutory functions and powers;

(5) failing to perform the food safety supervision and administration duties, thereby causing a food safety accident.

Article 145 In violation of the provisions of this Law, where the food safety supervision and administration, health administration, and agricultural administration departments of the people's government at or above the county level commit any of the following acts, causing adverse consequences, the directly responsible persons in charge and other directly liable persons shall be given the sanction of a warning, a demerit, or a major demerit; if the circumstances are relatively serious, the sanction of demotion or removal from office shall be given; if the circumstances are serious, the sanction of expulsion shall be given:

(1) after obtaining relevant food safety information, failing to report to the higher competent department and the people's government at the same level as required, or failing to notify each other as required;

(2) failing to publish food safety information as required;

(3) failing to perform statutory duties, failing to cooperate in the investigation and handling of food safety illegal acts, or abusing power, neglecting duties, or engaging in favoritism and malpractice.
